From 271167545b06f634cc4eee0d4cd8377356d36c44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:20:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] drama: long-form joins rest as the punctuation asks and
 keep one level

At each join the silence the model left (the earlier segment's tail and the
next one's head, in 10 ms frames under -42 dBFS) is measured, and only the
shortfall to the boundary's pause is added: 0.42 s after . or !, 0.48 s
after ?, 0.55 s after an ellipsis, 0.70 s at a blank line, 0.20 s inside a
sentence. The pause is the earlier segment's quietest tail stretch played
back and forth, or digital silence when it has no quiet tail. A segment
whose speech level is more than 1.5 dB from the earlier segments' median
gets one gain to 1.5 dB, at most 3 dB, never past a 0.99 peak. A blank line
always ends a segment. X-Long-Form-Segments points at each segment after
its pause. A stream sends segment 1 as it is made and each later segment
whole once its level and pause are known. Plain and one-segment replies are
unchanged.
